    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Double Well [N]\n\nThe quartic double well $V(x) = V_0(x^2 - 1)^2$ has minima at $x = \\pm 1$ separated by a barrier of height $V_0$. A particle confined to one well would have a ground state near $\\omega/2$, with $\\omega = \\sqrt{8V_0}$ the curvature frequency at a minimum. Tunnelling through the barrier couples the two wells and splits this level into a symmetric ground state and an antisymmetric first excited state. For $V_0 = 10$:",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "V_dw(V0, xv) := V0*(xv^2 - 1)^2$\n[h_dw, x_dw] : grid(-3, 3, 600)$\ndw_levels(V0, m) := eig_lowest(fd_hamiltonian(h_dw, map(lambda([xv], float(V_dw(V0, xv))), x_dw)), m)$\n[E_dw, v_dw] : dw_levels(10, 4)$\nprintf(true, \"Lowest levels: ~{~,5f ~}~%\", E_dw)$\nprintf(true, \"Single-well estimate omega/2 = ~,5f~%\", sqrt(80.0)/2)$\nprintf(true, \"Splitting E1 - E0 = ~,5f, tunnelling time pi/(E1 - E0) = ~,2f~%\",\n       E_dw[2] - E_dw[1], %pi/(E_dw[2] - E_dw[1]))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Lowest levels: 4.11341 4.23852 10.11061 12.25421\nSingle-well estimate omega/2 = 4.47214\nSplitting E1 - E0 = 0.12511, tunnelling time pi/(E1 - E0) = 25.11"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The two lowest states lie 0.13 apart, well below the barrier, while the next pair sits above it. A particle started in one well as $(\\psi_0 + \\psi_1)/\\sqrt 2$ moves to the other in time $\\pi/\\Delta E$. In the figure the two wavefunctions coincide in the right-hand well and have opposite signs in the left-hand one.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "inside_dw : sublist_indices(x_dw, lambda([xv], abs(xv) <= 2))$\nxs_dw : makelist(x_dw[i], i, inside_dw)$\nVl_dw : makelist(float(V_dw(10, xv)), xv, xs_dw)$\npsi_dw : makelist(to_psi(v_dw[j], h_dw), j, 1, 2)$\nax_draw2d(\n  level_objects(xs_dw, Vl_dw, firstn(E_dw, 2),\n                makelist(makelist(psi_dw[j][i], i, inside_dw), j, 1, 2), 1.5),\n  lines(xs_dw, Vl_dw, color = \"black\", dash = \"solid\", line_width = 3, name = \"V(x)\"),\n  title = \"Double Well, V0 = 10: Symmetric and Antisymmetric States\",\n  xlabel = \"x\", ylabel = \"E, and ψ offset by E\", yrange = [0, 12])$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 18,
      "outputs": [
        {
