      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Raising the barrier makes the splitting fall exponentially. The instanton (semiclassical) calculation predicts\n\n$$\\Delta E \\approx 2\\omega\\sqrt{\\frac{6S_0}{\\pi}}\\;e^{-S_0}, \\qquad S_0 = \\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2V(x)}\\,dx = \\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{2V_0},$$\n\nwhere $S_0$ is the tunnelling action under the barrier. The formula is the leading term of an expansion in $1/S_0$, so its ratio to the exact splitting should approach 1 as the barrier grows, with a shortfall of order $1/S_0$. First the action integral:",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "assume(V0 > 0)$\nS0 : integrate(sqrt(2*V0)*(1 - xv^2), xv, -1, 1);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 19,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "{{2^{{{5}\\over{2}}}\\,\\sqrt{V_{0}}}\\over{3}}"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 19,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The matrix splitting for barriers from 4 to 32, compared with the formula in a table and on a logarithmic axis:",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "dw_split(V0) := block([E : first(dw_levels(V0, 2))], E[2] - E[1])$\ninstanton(V0) := block([w : sqrt(8.0*V0), S : float(4/3*sqrt(2*V0))],\n  2*w*sqrt(6*S/%pi)*exp(-S))$\nbarriers : [4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32]$\nsplits : map(dw_split, barriers)$\nprintf(true, \" V0     S0     matrix dE    instanton    ratio   (1-ratio)*S0~%\")$\nfor j : 1 thru length(barriers) do block([V0 : barriers[j], S, r],\n  S : float(4/3*sqrt(2*V0)), r : splits[j]/float(instanton(V0)),\n  printf(true, \"~3d ~7,3f ~12,4e ~12,4e ~7,4f ~9,3f~%\", V0, S, splits[j], float(instanton(V0)), r, (1 - r)*S))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color = \"#1f77b4\", marker_size = 9, points(barriers, splits, name = \"matrix eigenvalues\"),\n  color = \"#d62728\", dash = \"dash\", line_width = 2,\n  explicit(instanton(V0), V0, 4, 32, name = \"instanton formula\"),\n  logy = true, title = \"Tunnelling Splitting of the Double Well\",\n  xlabel = \"barrier height V0\", ylabel = \"E1 - E0\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 20,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            " V0     S0     matrix dE    instanton    ratio   (1-ratio)*S0\n  4   3.771    4.6239e-1    6.9907e-1  0.6614     1.277\n  6   4.619    2.9711e-1    4.0597e-1  0.7318     1.239\n  8   5.333    1.9137e-1    2.4654e-1  0.7762     1.193\n 12   6.532    8.3282e-2    1.0078e-1  0.8264     1.134\n 16   7.542    3.8868e-2    4.5524e-2  0.8538     1.103\n 20   8.433    1.9255e-2    2.2094e-2  0.8715     1.084\n 24   9.238    1.0015e-2    1.1327e-2  0.8842     1.070\n 28   9.978    5.4216e-3    6.0658e-3  0.8938     1.060\n 32  10.667    3.0350e-3    3.3666e-3  0.9015     1.051"
          ]
        },
        {
